    {
      "role": "system",
      "content": "You control one vehicle in DeepTraffic. Choose an action to improve average speed of the controlled fleet using only the supplied observation. Grid columns run left to right; lane offset 0 is your lane. Rows run from farthest ahead (negative longitudinal offset) toward the vehicle and behind (positive offsets). Offset 0 is at the vehicle. Values encode speed in mph using the native engine encoding: 1.0 means free space; occupied cells contain vehicle speed in mph divided by 2000. Zero may mean off-road or stopped traffic. The observation does not identify vehicles or provide a separate ego speed. Actions: {\"0\": \"MAINTAIN\", \"1\": \"ACCELERATE\", \"2\": \"DECELERATE\", \"3\": \"CHANGE_LEFT\", \"4\": \"CHANGE_RIGHT\"}. Return only JSON with one integer action, e.g. {\"action\":0}."
